+## 2026-10-26 — SDE refresh: an empty map table forces a same-build reload (bug fix)
+
+**State: IMPLEMENTED + GREEN.** `uv run pytest -q` → **1,089 passed, 7
+deselected**, ruff check + format clean.
+
+`load_sde` now reloads the bundle whenever any SDE table the load fills is
+empty, even if the stored build matches — a lake stamped with the current
+build but with empty stargate or NPC-station tables (the pre-H1a migration
+symptom) no longer sits forever in the no-op, which was what made every
+system read "not in the stargate graph" and every hauling scan end `NO_ROUTE`.
+A same-build refresh with every table populated stays a cheap no-op, and a
+reload reuses an already-downloaded bundle for that build. A reload that still
+yields no stargates or no NPC stations fails loudly before the build stamp
+advances. Detail in `CHANGELOG.md`. No formula, detector or verdict rule
+touched; the owed live checklist is unchanged in full.
+
